WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.511 --> 00:00:03.790
- [Mark] Alright, Sergio.
- Yeah?

00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:05.010
- [Mark] Sergio, tell me about your life,

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:06.320
tell me where you grew up.

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:09.390
- [Sergio] Well, I grew up
right here by Echo Park.

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:11.170
(sirens and honking)

00:00:11.170 --> 00:00:14.180
Childhood was... normal I guess.

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:15.910
Both my parents were alcoholics,

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:22.630
so growing up there wasn't too
much supervision, you know?

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:25.680
So I got to do like, I mean,

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:28.100
I got to do whatever I wanted, stay out,

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:32.903
and they care, or they were
just too drunk to care.

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:39.080
Besides, I wouldn't want to be at home.

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:40.953
My dad would beat my mom, you know?

00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:46.810
So I, you know, I joined a gang.

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:48.730
- [Mark] What age?

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:51.630
- I was still in junior high,
so I think I was like 13.

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:52.463
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:00:52.463 --> 00:00:53.300
- 13.

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:54.450
- [Mark] Which gang?

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:55.410
- Headhunters.

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:56.243
- [Mark] Headhunters?

00:00:56.243 --> 00:00:57.186
- Yeah.

00:00:57.186 --> 00:00:58.019
- [Mark] That's a Hispanic gang?

00:00:58.019 --> 00:00:58.920
- It's a Hispanic gang, yeah.

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:04.120
And you know, I joined a gang.

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:07.677
I did what gang members do, you know?

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:14.612
I go to juvenile hall, my
first time I get arrested.

00:01:14.612 --> 00:01:16.812
I was like 15, I got
arrested for a firearm.

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:19.323
I get out.

00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:23.550
Then like a month later,
three weeks later,

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:26.510
I get arrested for attempted murder.

00:01:26.510 --> 00:01:29.160
It gets dropped down to
assault with a deadly weapon.

00:01:31.210 --> 00:01:32.660
I do like a year off for that

00:01:34.003 --> 00:01:37.182
in camp, juvenile camp.
(loud sirens)

00:01:37.182 --> 00:01:38.099
Then at 17,

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:41.363
at 17, I feel like,

00:01:43.050 --> 00:01:44.160
like I need money, you know?

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:47.070
Like I see all my other homies, like,

00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:49.693
you know, having to steal cars, whatever.

00:01:51.530 --> 00:01:52.683
So I wanted money, too.

00:01:53.749 --> 00:01:57.290
And the easiest way I could
make money, I had a gun,

00:01:57.290 --> 00:02:00.833
so the easiest way I could
make money is doing robberies.

00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:07.050
And so my first robbery,

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:09.243
I remember my first robbery was,

00:02:10.721 --> 00:02:12.640
it was a Little Caesars.

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:14.230
Those were my favorite targets,

00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:15.160
Little Caesars or Subways,

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:18.140
'cause they're always like
hidden, like in a cut.

00:02:18.140 --> 00:02:20.740
They're, you know, small
little establishments

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.903
where I could go by myself.

00:02:23.802 --> 00:02:24.830
In and out, right?

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:28.640
And so I remember the first one I was...

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:31.083
I did it, it was like,
I was nervous at first.

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:33.400
And then it just became easy.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:36.810
And then it just became
like, like too easy.

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:41.810
And it was never a lot of
money, $500, you know, 300.

00:02:43.046 --> 00:02:44.408
- [Mark] Yeah, but you
were getting away with it.

00:02:44.408 --> 00:02:46.029
- I was getting away with it, and...

00:02:46.029 --> 00:02:48.010
- [Mark] How many did you do?

00:02:48.010 --> 00:02:48.930
- Countless.
- [Mark] Really?

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:50.520
- Oh yeah.
- [Mark] Wow.

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:51.423
- At 18,

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:56.190
a month after my 18th birthday,

00:02:56.190 --> 00:02:59.743
I get arrested for robberies,
for doing those robberies.

00:03:03.634 --> 00:03:05.000
You know, I get caught with a gun.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:08.350
They're charging me for robberies.

00:03:08.350 --> 00:03:10.137
I mean, I'm 18 years old,
I just turned 18 years old.

00:03:10.137 --> 00:03:11.553
I'm in a County jail.

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:17.960
And so I'm fighting my case,

00:03:19.289 --> 00:03:22.420
they offer me 12 years
as a deal, as you know,

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:26.490
as a deal to take for the robberies.

00:03:26.490 --> 00:03:29.883
And I take it.

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:33.779
So I'm 18.

00:03:33.779 --> 00:03:35.480
I'm looking at 12 years.

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:38.720
For me, 12 years at 18
might as well had been life.

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:40.590
You know, like, I was doing the math.

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:43.333
I was, I'm gonna get out
when I'm 30, 30 something.

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:50.540
So I was there, and I was gonna,

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:53.568
I was going to walk on eggshells, right?

00:03:53.568 --> 00:03:56.243
So I get to prison,

00:03:57.520 --> 00:04:02.520
and I'm one of those
kids that wants to like,

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:04.630
wants to participate, you know?

00:04:04.630 --> 00:04:06.207
I believe in (foreign language),

00:04:08.370 --> 00:04:13.063
in our, the thing we have
established in prison, right?

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:17.823
Our Southern Hispanics.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:21.290
So...

00:04:23.450 --> 00:04:26.350
I started doing, I start, you
know, doing stuff in prison.

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:30.023
Little stabbings here,
little stabbings there.

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:35.873
I see...

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:41.940
I see one of my good friends, actually,

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:44.200
I used to work out with him in the yard.

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:47.600
He has to, you know, it's his turn.

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:51.750
It's his turn to go on a mission, right?

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:56.963
To earn his stripes or whatever.

00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:00.710
And so, during shower time, he...

00:05:00.710 --> 00:05:04.320
It's his celly who was actually
going to be the victim.

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:09.320
So they go out and, and there's a porter.

00:05:09.922 --> 00:05:12.570
They're like janitors, right?

00:05:12.570 --> 00:05:13.403
They're inmates.

00:05:16.226 --> 00:05:20.077
He calls my friend's
celly, calls him over.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:25.790
And when he's walking
over to him, my friend,

00:05:25.790 --> 00:05:29.150
he starts, you know,
stabbing him or whatever.

00:05:29.150 --> 00:05:31.430
They both start stabbing this guy.

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:32.990
And the tower, he's
running showers, right?

00:05:32.990 --> 00:05:33.840
So he's running showers,

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:35.960
he's doing this little shower thing.

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:38.260
And I guess he hears, like, locomotion.

00:05:38.260 --> 00:05:42.020
So he comes, he runs from
where he was at, C Section,

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:44.830
he runs to B Section with no...

00:05:48.430 --> 00:05:49.360
It was just...

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:57.150
I wouldn't even expect
it, but he gets his rifle,

00:05:57.150 --> 00:06:01.610
mini 14, and he shoots my buddy, you know?

00:06:01.610 --> 00:06:03.370
He shoots my buddy in the head.

00:06:03.370 --> 00:06:06.220
I remember just one
second seeing him do this

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:09.130
to his cellmate, and then the next second

00:06:09.130 --> 00:06:11.840
he was just on the floor.

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:12.673
- [Mark] And the guard shot him?

00:06:12.673 --> 00:06:15.832
- Yeah, the guard shot him,
shot him dead in the head.

00:06:15.832 --> 00:06:20.313
And my whole time, I had already
been in prison four years.

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:26.150
So my whole time in prison had
been like, yeah, this is fun.

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:28.850
But when that happened, I was like...

00:06:31.380 --> 00:06:32.213
Welcome to prison.

00:06:32.213 --> 00:06:35.140
You know, like, it had
finally hit me that, man,

00:06:35.140 --> 00:06:38.980
like, that could happen to me,

00:06:38.980 --> 00:06:42.210
'cause I do that kind of stuff, you know?

00:06:42.210 --> 00:06:47.210
So anyways, it just gave me
something to think about.

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:48.873
Anyway, so...

00:06:51.424 --> 00:06:53.263
You know, I continue my prison term.

00:06:54.170 --> 00:06:57.140
Like five years in, I still
need, like, seven years.

00:06:57.140 --> 00:06:58.750
Something like that.

00:06:58.750 --> 00:07:00.073
I'm in my early twenties.

00:07:05.942 --> 00:07:09.320
So yeah, there's this big guy, right?

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:11.410
He a big homie.

00:07:11.410 --> 00:07:13.953
He needs, he asks me for a favor.

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:18.900
And those are the kinds of
guys that you, you're like,

00:07:18.900 --> 00:07:20.270
this is who you bleed for, you know?

00:07:20.270 --> 00:07:22.850
Like, they tell you to
do something, you do it.

00:07:22.850 --> 00:07:25.443
Because, you know, they're
the big dogs, right?

00:07:26.680 --> 00:07:30.140
So I was like, I'm like, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:07:30.140 --> 00:07:31.733
I'm flattered and whatnot.

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:38.220
So, you know.

00:07:38.220 --> 00:07:43.220
It was summertime, it was
like 2009, 2010 summertime.

00:07:44.800 --> 00:07:45.673
Hot as hell.

00:07:46.870 --> 00:07:50.480
And, you know, I see my victim.

00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:52.723
Some guy from somewhere.

00:07:54.820 --> 00:07:58.453
Me and my crimey, the one
I was gonna do it with,

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:03.910
we see him getting out of work.

00:08:03.910 --> 00:08:05.350
'Cause he worked at the Program Office.

00:08:05.350 --> 00:08:07.283
You know, like, typing stuff out.

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:12.020
And so...

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:19.450
We, when he's about to
go inside the building,

00:08:19.450 --> 00:08:24.450
in the prison yard, we just
start attacking him, you know?

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:27.690
And I remember feeling tired.

00:08:27.690 --> 00:08:30.883
I remember while I was,

00:08:32.860 --> 00:08:33.870
while we were stabbing him, like,

00:08:33.870 --> 00:08:36.577
I remember like, thinking,

00:08:36.577 --> 00:08:38.612
"Man, where the fuck is the cops at?

00:08:38.612 --> 00:08:41.603
"Why haven't they rang the alarm yet?

00:08:43.007 --> 00:08:44.230
"Why haven't they rang the alarm?"

00:08:44.230 --> 00:08:45.830
I was so tired.

00:08:45.830 --> 00:08:49.320
I remember sweating
and just tired as hell.

00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:51.381
And I was like, wondering where the f-...

00:08:51.381 --> 00:08:53.020
Like, it doesn't, it
shouldn't take this long

00:08:53.020 --> 00:08:55.129
for the alarm to sound, you know?

00:08:55.129 --> 00:08:57.417
And it finally sounds.
(mimics prison alarm)

00:08:57.417 --> 00:08:59.630
And I still can't stop until
I get sprayed, you know?

00:08:59.630 --> 00:09:02.993
So I see these correction
officers running toward me.

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:05.600
And when they're about to spray me, like,

00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:08.723
I try to throw them the
shank, the prison shank.

00:09:09.730 --> 00:09:10.563
I try to throw it.

00:09:10.563 --> 00:09:12.290
Anyways, I get pepper sprayed.

00:09:12.290 --> 00:09:14.323
This guy, he gets stepped 37 times.

00:09:15.710 --> 00:09:17.000
I go to seg.

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:19.920
After that, they sent me
to the hole, of course.

00:09:19.920 --> 00:09:24.653
Then I go to a segregated
housing unit for three years.

00:09:26.360 --> 00:09:27.193
For three years.

00:09:29.461 --> 00:09:32.400
And so for three years I
was in a cell by myself.

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:33.520
I'll go to yard.

00:09:33.520 --> 00:09:37.913
My yard was a cage, like
a dog kennel cage, right?

00:09:39.451 --> 00:09:40.990
It was smaller than my cell.

00:09:40.990 --> 00:09:44.000
Just enough so I could
pace back and forth.

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:46.968
Like, maybe like, three
steps this way, you know.

00:09:46.968 --> 00:09:47.801
And probably like nine steps that way.

00:09:47.801 --> 00:09:49.660
I don't know. It was small, right?

00:09:49.660 --> 00:09:51.510
Anyways, we're all going to the yard.

00:09:54.470 --> 00:09:55.303
So I'm just there.

00:09:55.303 --> 00:09:58.710
And for three years,
reading, that's all I did.

00:09:58.710 --> 00:10:00.110
Read books.

00:10:00.110 --> 00:10:02.110
Read books and watch a little bit of TV.

00:10:05.920 --> 00:10:06.860
I got released.

00:10:06.860 --> 00:10:09.993
I got released from the seg
housing unit, I go back to GP.

00:10:12.990 --> 00:10:17.340
My last two years in prison,
I started doing drugs.

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:18.450
I don't know why.

00:10:18.450 --> 00:10:21.310
I was like so close to my
release, it was so close.

00:10:21.310 --> 00:10:22.143
I started doing drugs.

00:10:22.143 --> 00:10:24.700
I started doing heroin.

00:10:24.700 --> 00:10:26.303
Heroin and crystal in prison.

00:10:28.430 --> 00:10:33.430
And the prison, like,
you're either going to eat,

00:10:33.640 --> 00:10:34.473
or you're going to do drugs.

00:10:34.473 --> 00:10:36.429
You can't do both, you know?

00:10:36.429 --> 00:10:39.863
So I was getting myself in debt.

00:10:40.980 --> 00:10:43.120
Getting myself in debt and debt and debt.

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:44.970
And as a Southern Hispanic guy,

00:10:44.970 --> 00:10:48.520
I can't buy drugs from any other race.

00:10:48.520 --> 00:10:50.420
I could buy drugs from the white people,

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:52.750
but not from a black, not from...

00:10:52.750 --> 00:10:54.100
You know, it's very racial.

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:56.660
And so, but I'm not giving a fuck.

00:10:56.660 --> 00:10:57.493
I'm not giving a fuck.

00:10:57.493 --> 00:11:00.580
I'm buying drugs from whoever
sells it to me, right?

00:11:00.580 --> 00:11:05.463
And I'm like, so close to going home.

00:11:08.173 --> 00:11:09.780
Because the whole time in prison,

00:11:09.780 --> 00:11:12.220
I had lived my life in prison

00:11:12.220 --> 00:11:13.760
not thinking about my
release date, you know?

00:11:13.760 --> 00:11:17.233
Like I was just doing it as if
I didn't have a release date.

00:11:19.900 --> 00:11:21.993
Thinking back now, I'm like, wow.

00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:28.960
I can't... I don't think I'd
be able to do that shit, again.

00:11:28.960 --> 00:11:31.923
But anyways, I racked up like a $700 debt.

00:11:32.930 --> 00:11:35.870
And in prison, that's a
lot of money, you know?

00:11:35.870 --> 00:11:38.370
Especially if you're
owning all types of races.

00:11:38.370 --> 00:11:40.300
Now your own people want
to get you, you know?

00:11:40.300 --> 00:11:42.650
'Cause you're breaking the rules.

00:11:42.650 --> 00:11:45.373
So I'll be at yard.

00:11:48.890 --> 00:11:52.070
A year left in my prison
term, my 12 year prison term.

00:11:52.070 --> 00:11:55.033
And I remember like having a, you know,

00:11:56.270 --> 00:11:57.737
every day before going to yard I would

00:11:57.737 --> 00:12:01.480
put a fucking knife up my
ass, and go to the yard,

00:12:01.480 --> 00:12:04.480
and go to the pisser, pretend
like I'm taking a piss.

00:12:04.480 --> 00:12:05.857
Look up at the tower, make
sure he's not looking at me.

00:12:05.857 --> 00:12:07.950
Pull that mother fucker out,

00:12:07.950 --> 00:12:11.240
and tie it up to my
shorts, my draw string.

00:12:11.240 --> 00:12:13.820
And I remember being, like
walking around the track,

00:12:13.820 --> 00:12:16.380
in prison, and looking
at my people, right?

00:12:16.380 --> 00:12:18.393
The Southern Hispanics, and thinking like,

00:12:19.747 --> 00:12:22.965
"Which one of those is going
to be the ones to get me?"

00:12:22.965 --> 00:12:26.103
For, you know, doing what I was doing.

00:12:27.470 --> 00:12:32.470
But, you know, thank goodness
nothing came out of that.

00:12:32.500 --> 00:12:36.863
I had my celly actually,
he helped me pay the debt.

00:12:39.560 --> 00:12:42.620
Like, like the day I went,
the day before I got released.

00:12:42.620 --> 00:12:43.453
- [Mark] Wow, that's nice of him.

00:12:43.453 --> 00:12:44.750
- Yeah, the day before.

00:12:44.750 --> 00:12:46.957
'Cause I was, cause I told him like,

00:12:46.957 --> 00:12:49.437
"Hey, I owe this money."

00:12:49.437 --> 00:12:52.630
And I didn't wanna, I didn't
want to leave the prison yard

00:12:53.930 --> 00:12:56.920
feeling like I had to sneak
away like a weasel, you know?

00:12:56.920 --> 00:13:00.490
Like, I had a debt and I couldn't pay it.

00:13:00.490 --> 00:13:02.790
But I was going to try it, you know?

00:13:02.790 --> 00:13:06.993
And so I'm telling my celly about it.

00:13:07.940 --> 00:13:09.220
And he's, you know, he's in prison.

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:13.120
He does his little hustles
in prison, so he had money.

00:13:13.120 --> 00:13:17.860
He pays my debt, you know,
the day before I got released.

00:13:17.860 --> 00:13:18.750
So...

00:13:23.140 --> 00:13:26.970
I walk out the cell, like, not feeling...

00:13:26.970 --> 00:13:28.610
Because who knows, I
could've came back, you know?

00:13:28.610 --> 00:13:30.150
I was going to get out,
there's no telling,

00:13:30.150 --> 00:13:31.000
I could come back, and what?

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:32.720
I still gonna owe that money, you know?

00:13:32.720 --> 00:13:34.593
Anyway, so I get released.

00:13:37.140 --> 00:13:42.140
And I start my new life out
here in the streets, again.

00:13:44.410 --> 00:13:48.020
The last time I had been
out here was when I was 18.

00:13:48.020 --> 00:13:51.170
Now I'm 31, not knowing
what the fuck to do.

00:13:51.170 --> 00:13:52.420
Both my parents are dead.

00:13:54.130 --> 00:13:55.853
My brother's down in San Diego.

00:13:59.250 --> 00:14:00.450
So what can I do, right?

00:14:02.260 --> 00:14:04.070
I have no work history.

00:14:04.070 --> 00:14:06.210
I never had a job in my life.

00:14:06.210 --> 00:14:08.210
Other than the little prison ones I had.

00:14:09.190 --> 00:14:10.620
The ones in prison, I mean.

00:14:13.350 --> 00:14:15.983
So it was a struggle, right?

00:14:21.470 --> 00:14:24.890
The only thing I could do
is sell drugs, you know.

00:14:24.890 --> 00:14:26.380
I'm not trying to do no more robberies.

00:14:26.380 --> 00:14:28.800
They gave me 12 years on
the first one, you know?

00:14:28.800 --> 00:14:32.980
So I see selling drugs as...

00:14:35.720 --> 00:14:38.100
less of a risk, less risky.

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:40.050
You know, do less time if I get caught.

00:14:43.850 --> 00:14:44.683
So...

00:14:46.210 --> 00:14:48.450
I was, that's how I was surviving

00:14:48.450 --> 00:14:50.243
for the first year I was out.

00:14:51.310 --> 00:14:53.400
Until like, until I got arrested.

00:14:53.400 --> 00:14:56.980
I got arrested a year
later after I get released.

00:14:56.980 --> 00:15:00.840
And they gave me four years for a firearm

00:15:00.840 --> 00:15:05.343
and having possession of
controlled substance, crystal meth.

00:15:06.290 --> 00:15:08.373
So now I'm in my second prison term.

00:15:09.400 --> 00:15:12.700
I'm 32 years old, have to do four years.

00:15:12.700 --> 00:15:16.900
And I'm like, you know, like
I'm back in prison, you know?

00:15:16.900 --> 00:15:19.700
A place that I didn't think
I was going to come back to.

00:15:23.460 --> 00:15:26.377
I go to prison, and I was at Calipatria.

00:15:27.330 --> 00:15:29.570
My first month there...

00:15:29.570 --> 00:15:32.980
Like I had done 12 years
and yeah, I would see a lot

00:15:32.980 --> 00:15:35.623
of people get stabbed and
stuff like that, beat up.

00:15:36.510 --> 00:15:40.880
But like, other than
probably like two people

00:15:40.880 --> 00:15:43.427
that actually got killed
in the 12 years that I did,

00:15:43.427 --> 00:15:45.910
like that I seen, actually,
that I'd actually seen?

00:15:45.910 --> 00:15:47.575
Two people who got killed.

00:15:47.575 --> 00:15:49.943
In this prison I was in, in Calipatria,

00:15:51.470 --> 00:15:54.170
my first month there some guy died,

00:15:54.170 --> 00:15:57.467
some guy gets stabbed to death, right?

00:15:57.467 --> 00:15:59.197
And they don't put us lockdown.

00:15:59.197 --> 00:16:03.423
They resume program like a few days later.

00:16:03.423 --> 00:16:05.280
And the following week, another guy dies.

00:16:05.280 --> 00:16:07.490
And I'm thinking like, all right,

00:16:07.490 --> 00:16:10.010
I've only been here like
a month, month and a half.

00:16:10.010 --> 00:16:11.750
And two people already died.

00:16:11.750 --> 00:16:14.000
Like, where the fuck am I at, right?

00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:17.910
Like, I only got four years
to do, like, you know?

00:16:21.340 --> 00:16:23.393
But I believe in this
shit, though, you know?

00:16:24.887 --> 00:16:27.940
I sacrificed a lot for,
you know, for this.

00:16:29.310 --> 00:16:32.160
But it's something... I think
about it, though, you know?

00:16:33.640 --> 00:16:35.820
And so, in those yards, like,

00:16:35.820 --> 00:16:37.093
everybody participates, you know?

00:16:37.093 --> 00:16:40.883
There's no like, "Oh,
I'll pass," you know?

00:16:40.883 --> 00:16:43.033
Nah, you're there, you
have to participate.

00:16:43.960 --> 00:16:44.793
So...

00:16:46.250 --> 00:16:47.083
I'm there.

00:16:47.083 --> 00:16:49.363
I'm just trying to lay
low for the most part.

00:16:52.802 --> 00:16:53.635
And yeah.

00:16:56.150 --> 00:16:57.600
Nothing much happens, like...

00:17:00.730 --> 00:17:02.970
To think about it, that was
like the most violent prison

00:17:02.970 --> 00:17:05.060
I had been to, like ever.

00:17:05.060 --> 00:17:07.690
And I've been to like
nine different prisons.

00:17:07.690 --> 00:17:09.440
That was like the most violent one.

00:17:12.910 --> 00:17:15.323
I've been out from that
term, from my second term.

00:17:15.323 --> 00:17:20.323
I've already been out
six months, seven months.

00:17:23.350 --> 00:17:24.880
So now I'm just...

00:17:24.880 --> 00:17:26.410
I'm just out here trying
to survive, you know?

00:17:26.410 --> 00:17:27.760
- [Mark] So you've been out a while now?

00:17:27.760 --> 00:17:31.867
- Like almost a year, like
not quite a year, yet.

00:17:34.820 --> 00:17:36.623
- [Mark] You still have
contact with your gang?

00:17:38.710 --> 00:17:39.543
- Yeah.

00:17:41.925 --> 00:17:44.003
That's the only family you have, you know?

00:17:44.940 --> 00:17:48.690
Those are the only family I have.

00:17:48.690 --> 00:17:51.017
Like there's, I have no other family.

00:17:52.620 --> 00:17:57.620
And there are a few, not
a lot, not a lot of it.

00:17:58.167 --> 00:18:01.693
And so I, I hold on to that, you know?

00:18:06.130 --> 00:18:11.060
I'm 35 years old and I'm
walking around baldheaded

00:18:11.060 --> 00:18:16.040
with tattoos everywhere still, you know?

00:18:16.040 --> 00:18:18.810
I'm not saying I'm out there gang banging,

00:18:18.810 --> 00:18:22.250
but I still represent who I am, you know?

00:18:22.250 --> 00:18:23.750
Because that's all I have.

00:18:23.750 --> 00:18:24.650
That's all I have.

00:18:26.700 --> 00:18:27.700
I have nothing else.

00:18:32.310 --> 00:18:33.560
- [Mark] Do you regret...

00:18:34.810 --> 00:18:38.200
Do you regret taking that
direction in life, years ago?

00:18:38.200 --> 00:18:41.203
- I mean, if I could do it all over again,

00:18:43.452 --> 00:18:48.452
I would do some things
different, you know.

00:18:48.540 --> 00:18:49.440
But out...

00:18:52.160 --> 00:18:54.242
- [Mark] There weren't a
lot of options for you.

00:18:54.242 --> 00:18:56.494
- There not...
- [Mark] In that neighborhood.

00:18:56.494 --> 00:18:57.963
For that neighborhood, for
the neighborhood you grew up.

00:19:00.652 --> 00:19:02.503
- Yeah, yeah. There was no option.

00:19:04.340 --> 00:19:07.432
- [Mark] There was no doctor,
lawyer, role models like that.

00:19:07.432 --> 00:19:08.265
- Nah.

00:19:11.430 --> 00:19:12.723
And me as a drop out...

00:19:19.111 --> 00:19:24.111
So I just, I joined the street gang.

00:19:26.180 --> 00:19:29.623
Now I'm 35 years old thinking
like, fuck, is this it?

00:19:35.390 --> 00:19:36.223
But I love it though.

00:19:36.223 --> 00:19:37.168
Like, I love it.

00:19:37.168 --> 00:19:41.533
I wouldn't trade this for anything.

00:19:42.770 --> 00:19:44.780
I wouldn't trade this shit for nothing.

00:19:44.780 --> 00:19:49.130
I rather be out here fuckin' in skid row

00:19:49.130 --> 00:19:51.683
then in prison any day, you know?

00:19:54.230 --> 00:19:56.093
So I'm grateful for that.

00:20:04.702 --> 00:20:05.983
- [Mark] And you have no kids?

00:20:07.000 --> 00:20:08.663
- I actually have my first.

00:20:10.540 --> 00:20:13.820
I have one, a son, he's a newborn.

00:20:13.820 --> 00:20:14.653
- [Mark] Oh really?

00:20:14.653 --> 00:20:15.560
- Yeah, he's a newborn.

00:20:15.560 --> 00:20:18.200
But I...

00:20:21.760 --> 00:20:22.860
Not really, I haven't been.

00:20:22.860 --> 00:20:25.220
Like, I tried, but I haven't been.

00:20:25.220 --> 00:20:29.110
CPS, Child Protective, they took the kid.

00:20:29.110 --> 00:20:33.630
Because the mother of
my baby, she got caught.

00:20:33.630 --> 00:20:35.960
You know, she tested
dirty when she gave birth,

00:20:35.960 --> 00:20:40.050
she was under the influence
of drugs, you know?

00:20:40.050 --> 00:20:41.243
So they took the baby.

00:20:44.210 --> 00:20:45.043
And...

00:20:47.570 --> 00:20:48.403
It's been tough.

00:20:52.479 --> 00:20:55.320
And you know, there's no way.

00:20:55.320 --> 00:20:58.330
Right now, I can't...

00:21:00.010 --> 00:21:01.340
I can't get my baby back right now.

00:21:01.340 --> 00:21:02.173
The way I'm living?

00:21:02.173 --> 00:21:04.480
Like I don't have... you know?

00:21:04.480 --> 00:21:05.313
So...

00:21:08.730 --> 00:21:09.563
Yeah, it's...

00:21:11.300 --> 00:21:12.133
I know he's safe.

00:21:12.133 --> 00:21:13.633
I know he's... he's good.

00:21:15.605 --> 00:21:18.250
It's just...

00:21:24.460 --> 00:21:27.450
If I do have any regrets,
it's that, you know?

00:21:27.450 --> 00:21:29.253
Not being there for my son.

00:21:30.720 --> 00:21:31.970
As I should be, you know.

00:21:35.552 --> 00:21:36.860
It fills me with shame.

00:21:36.860 --> 00:21:40.430
Like, you know, even my
parents, my parents were drunks,

00:21:40.430 --> 00:21:44.660
they were drunks, alcoholics, but...

00:21:47.610 --> 00:21:49.000
They, you know, they...

00:21:51.470 --> 00:21:53.957
When I needed them, they
were there, you know?

00:21:54.820 --> 00:21:55.700
When I needed...

00:21:55.700 --> 00:21:58.693
And to think that I
can't do that for my son.

00:22:00.870 --> 00:22:02.237
It's tough, you know.

00:22:05.177 --> 00:22:06.980
- [Mark] Are you using?
- Yeah.

00:22:06.980 --> 00:22:08.860
- [Mark] Currently? Which one?

00:22:08.860 --> 00:22:10.750
- Man, I'm doing it all, man.

00:22:11.716 --> 00:22:12.970
(sirens blaring)

00:22:12.970 --> 00:22:14.733
Cocaine, crystal.

00:22:17.500 --> 00:22:18.333
PCP.

00:22:19.965 --> 00:22:21.560
A little bit of heroin. A little bit.

00:22:21.560 --> 00:22:23.060
I really don't like that high.

00:22:26.360 --> 00:22:27.193
But...

00:22:32.050 --> 00:22:34.910
At first, I used to do drugs

00:22:34.910 --> 00:22:38.953
because it felt good and
it was fun, you know?

00:22:40.130 --> 00:22:43.200
Now I do the drugs just to...

00:22:44.550 --> 00:22:49.447
Just to not feel, you know?

00:22:51.160 --> 00:22:55.740
Just to like... ah, who cares?

00:22:55.740 --> 00:22:57.140
It could be worse, you know?

00:23:02.210 --> 00:23:05.180
So yeah, it helps.

00:23:05.180 --> 00:23:06.013
It helps.

00:23:06.013 --> 00:23:06.860
It's cold out there.

00:23:07.770 --> 00:23:09.220
It's cold out there at night.

00:23:11.520 --> 00:23:14.713
And you know, doing a little bit of meth,

00:23:15.770 --> 00:23:17.220
slamming a little bit of meth

00:23:18.330 --> 00:23:19.830
warms me up, you know, it really does.

00:23:19.830 --> 00:23:21.640
It makes me sweat, you know?

00:23:21.640 --> 00:23:24.202
Be like three in the morning
and I'm sweating, you know?

00:23:24.202 --> 00:23:25.552
'Cause it's cold out there.

00:23:28.331 --> 00:23:29.164
And yeah.

00:23:37.090 --> 00:23:37.923
I'm a good worker,

00:23:37.923 --> 00:23:39.403
I found out I'm good at work.

00:23:41.380 --> 00:23:42.213
I like working.

00:23:43.560 --> 00:23:48.173
But can't get hired anywhere.

00:23:53.840 --> 00:23:54.673
- [Mark] All right Sergio.

00:23:54.673 --> 00:23:56.913
Well, thank you so much for
coming and talking with me.

00:23:58.446 --> 00:23:59.279
Thank you.

